            <div xml:id="d467-a1">

                <pb facs="0850" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg788"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 8.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Law fixing the permanent force in the
                    army.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of War—Law.</hi></placeName>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Don Alfonso XII, by the grace of God, constitutional King of Spain. To all whom
                    the present may concern:</p>
                <p>Know that the Còrtes have decreed and we sanctioned the following: <list>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 1. The force of the permanent
                            army of the Peninsula for the economical year of 1878–1879 is fixed at
                            100,000.</item>
                        <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art</hi>. 2. The force of the army of the
                            island of Cuba shall be that which may be considered necessary in order
                            to complete the pacification of the said Antilla. That of the armies of
                            Porto Rico and Philippine Islands for the next economical year shall
                            consist of 3,751 and 10,475 men respectively.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Therefore we command all the tribunals, justices, chiefs, governors, and other
                    authorities, civil as well as military and ecclesiastic of any class or dignity,
                    to keep and cause to be kept, to fulfill and execute the present law in all its
                    parts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Given at the palace on <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-04-22">this the 22d day of April,
                            1878</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> I, the King.<lb/>The minister of war.<lb/><signed>FRANCISCO
                        CEBALLOS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
